## GPU Programming with XIOM

### The Vulkan Pipeline

```
Application
  ↓
Vertex Shader   → Transforms vertices
  ↓
Rasterizer      → Converts to fragments
  ↓
Fragment Shader → Colors each pixel
  ↓
Framebuffer     → Display on screen
```

### XIOM Vulkan Setup

```xiom
use xiom.vulkan;

fn main() -> Int {
  // Initialize Vulkan
  let instance = vulkan::Instance::new()?;
  let surface = vulkan::Surface::new(&instance, window)?;

  // Select GPU
  let physical_device = instance.select_gpu(surface)?;
  let device = vulkan::Device::new(&physical_device)?;

  // Create swapchain for double/triple buffering
  let swapchain = vulkan::Swapchain::new(&device, &surface)?;

  // Main render loop
  while !window.should_close() {
    let frame = swapchain.acquire_next_image()?;
    render_frame(&device, &frame);
    swapchain.present(&frame);
  }
  return 0;
}
```

### Memory Management

```xiom
// Allocate GPU buffer
let buffer = vulkan::Buffer::new(
  &device,
  size: 1024,
  usage: BufferUsage::Vertex | BufferUsage::TransferDst,
  memory: MemoryProperty::DeviceLocal,
);

// Map and write data
buffer.map(|ptr| {
  ptr.write(vertex_data);
});
```

### Pipeline Creation

```xiom
// Graphics pipeline configuration
let pipeline = vulkan::GraphicsPipeline::new()
  .vertex_shader(compile_glsl("shader.vert"))
  .fragment_shader(compile_glsl("shader.frag"))
  .input_assembly(Topology::TriangleList)
  .viewport(0, 0, 800, 600)
  .rasterizer(CullMode::Back, FrontFace::Clockwise)
  .build(&device)?;
```

### Use Cases

- Real-time 3D rendering (games)
- GPU compute (machine learning, physics)
- Video processing
- Scientific visualization
- CAD and 3D modeling

